  "live_records": {
    "q-161945": {
      "dom_id": "step-q161945",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "$8÷(-3)$ is equivalent to",
      "worked_solution": "We have to divide a positive number $(8)$ by a negative one $(-3).$ So the result will be negative:\n\n$$\n8÷(-3)=-\\,\\boxed{}\n$$\n\nTo write down the number that goes in the box, recall that \n\n$$\n8÷3=\\frac{8}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n8÷(-3)=-\\frac{8}{3}.\n$$",
