      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "$(-4)÷9$ is equivalent to",
      "worked_solution": "Here, we are dividing a negative number $(-4)$ by a positive one $(9).$ So the result will be negative:\n\n$$\n(-4)÷9=-\\,\\boxed{}\n$$\n\nTo write down the fraction that goes in the box, recall that \n\n$$\n4÷9=\\frac{4}{9}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n(-4)÷9=-\\frac{4}{9}.\n$$",
