    "q-161942": {
      "dom_id": "step-q161942",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "$2÷(-9)$ is equivalent to",
      "worked_solution": "We have to divide a positive number $(2)$ by a negative one $(-9).$ So the result will be negative:\n\n$$\n2÷(-9)=-\\,\\boxed{}\n$$\n\nTo write down the number that goes in the box, recall that \n\n$$\n2÷9=\\frac{2}{9}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n2÷(-9)=-\\frac{2}{9}.\n$$",
