      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "$13÷(-6)$ is equivalent to",
      "worked_solution": "Here, we are dividing a positive number $(13)$ by a negative one $(-6).$ So the result will be negative:\n\n$$\n13÷(-6)=-\\,\\boxed{}\n$$\n\nNow, to write down the fraction that goes in the box, recall that\n\n$$\n13÷6=2\\,\\text{R}\\,1=2\\,\\frac{1}{6}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n13÷(-6)=-2\\,\\frac{1}{6}.\n$$",
