    "q-162114": {
      "dom_id": "step-q162114",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "$7÷(-4)$ is equivalent to",
      "worked_solution": "Here, we are dividing a positive number $(7)$ by a negative one $(-4).$ So the result will be negative:\n\n$$\n7÷(-4)=-\\,\\boxed{}\n$$\n\nNow, to write down the fraction that goes in the box, recall that\n\n$$\n7÷4=1\\,\\text{R}\\,3=1\\,\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n7÷(-4)=-1\\,\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-162114-a",
