    "q-162136": {
      "dom_id": "step-q162136",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "What is the missing part of the expression below?\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{19}=\\frac{\\bbox[1pt,border: 1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}}}{-19}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "A positive number can be obtained if we divide two numbers that are either both positive or both negative.\n\nSo, given a positive fraction, we have the following equivalent notations:\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{19}=\\frac{-4}{-19}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we see that the denominator on the right-hand side is negative $(-19).$ Therefore, the missing numerator must be $(-4):$\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{19}=\\frac{-4}{-19}\n$$",
